{"type":"standard","title":"Samwe language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Samwe language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3914052","titles":{"canonical":"Samwe_language","normalized":"Samwe language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Samwe language</span></span>"},"pageid":32250002,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1330691871","tid":"0aa8cc25-e766-11f0-b7f2-10d37d204b79","timestamp":"2026-01-01T23:03:10Z","description":"Gur language of Burkina","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samwe_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samwe_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samwe_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Samwe_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samwe_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Samwe_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samwe_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Samwe_language"}},"extract":"Samwé (samoe), also known as Wara, is a Gur language of Burkina Faso. Dialects are Negueni-Klani, Ouatourou-Niasogoni, and Soulani. Niasogoni speakers have difficulty with Negueni, but not vice versa.","extract_html":"<p><b>Samwé</b> (samoe), also known as <b>Wara</b>, is a Gur language of Burkina Faso. Dialects are Negueni-Klani, Ouatourou-Niasogoni, and Soulani. Niasogoni speakers have difficulty with Negueni, but not vice versa.</p>"}